    "updated_at": "2021-11-20T10:21:27Z",
    "body": "For JS apps I think it would be ok to have one-copy getImageData API. It solves only one problem - unnecessary memory allocation on every call of it (and as a consequence higher load for GC). It's nice if at some point we'd be able to have some kind of zero-copy API, but as @junov stated - it might be very tricky to have it even designed (it'd be a shared memory between browser internals and JS/WASM - that I find to be quite dangerous).",
